  "answer": "The goal was not met: only 2 of the 5 cases were confirmed, on two scenes. In both, VaVAM with the linear MPC failed every run at 1.2x hand-off speed (S1 on 02eadd92 and S3 on 054b5901). The failure ranges sit above 0.5 but are wide, because each rests on only a few runs. Neither case is really about the crossing car's timing. On 054b5901 the ego ignored a RIGHT command and drove onto the median with no other car involved, whether the crossing car was shifted or not. On 02eadd92 the ego drifted left into the oncoming bus at the recorded timing; no other timing was tried there. All of these failures are flagged as possible simulator artifacts because the ego ended more than 3.5 m off the recorded path. Triage found that the policy steered off course first and the camera view was clean before each failure, so they look like the policy's errors, not rendering. Scene 13a9767e came close to the crossing car many times across timings and speeds but never failed, and the other three scenes showed nothing.",
